  "working": "Identify geometry and hybridisation: [Fe(C2O4)3]3- octahedral (oxalate bidentate) → d2sp3 (or sp3d2) not sp3. [CuCl4]2- typically tetrahedral (Cl monodentate) → sp3 hybridisation; Cu2+ d9 high spin → paramagnetic (one unpaired). [Ni(CO)4] tetrahedral (CO strong field) Ni0 d10 → diamagnetic but geometry tetrahedral uses sp3? Ni(0) uses dsp2? Actually Ni(CO)4 is tetrahedral with dsp2? CO is strong field, Ni(0) d10, hybridisation often considered sp3? Usually tetrahedral complexes of d10 use sp3. But diamagnetic yes. [Zn(CN)4]2- tetrahedral (Zn2+ d10) → diamagnetic sp3. [Co(CN)6]3- octahedral low spin Co(III) d6 low spin → diamagnetic? Co(III) low spin d6 t2g6 → diamagnetic, but octahedral uses d2sp3 not sp3. [Co(NH3)6]3+ octahedral low spin Co(III) d6 → diamagnetic, not sp3. [Mn(H2O)6]2+ octahedral high spin d5 → paramagnetic. [Cr(NH3)6]3+ octahedral high spin d3 → paramagnetic. [Cu(CN)4]3- tetrahedral Cu(II) d9 → paramagnetic. [Fe(CN)6]4- octahedral low spin Fe(II) d6 → diamagnetic but not sp3. So diamagnetic species with sp3 hybridisation: need tetrahedral geometry and d10 or low spin d6? sp3 hybridisation typically for tetrahedral complexes (four ligands). Among list, tetrahedral complexes: [CuCl4]2-, [Ni(CO)4], [Zn(CN)4]2-, [Cu(CN)4]3- (maybe). Check diamagnetism: [CuCl4]2- Cu2+ d9 → paramagnetic (one unpaired). [Ni(CO)4] Ni0 d10 → diamagnetic, tetrahedral sp3? Ni(CO)4 is tetrahedral, hybridisation sp3 (or dsp2?). Usually Ni(CO)4 uses sp3 hybridisation (four CO ligands). [Zn(CN)4]2- Zn2+ d10 → diamagnetic, tetrahedral sp3. [Cu(CN)4]3- Cu(I) d10? Cu(I) is d10, tetrahedral? Usually Cu(I) complexes are tetrahedral or square planar; [Cu(CN)4]3- likely tetrahedral d10 diamagnetic. However need confirm typical hybridisation: tetrahedral complexes use sp3 hybridisation of central atom. So diamagnetic tetrahedral species: Ni(CO)4, Zn(CN)4^2-, Cu(CN)4^3- (if Cu(I) d10). [Fe(C2O4)3]3- octahedral not sp3. Others octahedral not sp3. Thus count = 3? But need ensure Cu(CN)4^3- is diamagnetic: Cu(I) d10 yes. So total 3. However some may consider Ni(CO)4 uses dsp2? But typical hybridisation for tetrahedral is sp3. So answer 3.",
