  "working": "Warming oxalate ion (C2O4^2-) with MnO2 in conc. H2SO4 leads to oxidation of oxalate to CO2 (common reaction). Thus <X> = CO2. Reaction of CO2 with water yields carbonic acid H2C2O4 (oxalic acid), which is a dibasic acid (can donate two protons). The carbon in CO2 is linear (sp hybridized), not bent. The carbon in H2C2O4 (oxalic acid) is trigonal planar around the carbonyl carbon? Actually oxalic acid has two carbonyl groups; each carbonyl carbon is trigonal planar (sp2). Thus <Y> (oxalic acid) has trigonal planar geometry around the carbonyl carbon(s). The hybridisation of carbon in CO2 (X) is sp, not sp2. Therefore options: (A) Y is a dibasic acid → true. (B) X has a bent shape around C → false (CO2 linear). (C) Y has a trigonal planar shape around C → true (carbonyl carbon). (D) The hybridisation state of C in X is sp2 → false (sp). Correct options: A and C.",
