  "working": "Red hot coke (carbon) reacts with steam (H₂O) at high temperature to produce carbon monoxide (CO) and hydrogen (H₂) according to the water-gas reaction: C + H₂O → CO + H₂. Thus <G> = CO. Treatment of CO with Cl₂ in the presence of sunlight/catalyst yields phosgene (COCl₂). Therefore <R> = COCl₂. CO has a triple bond (bond order 3), making option B correct. COCl₂ has a trigonal planar geometry (sp² hybridisation at carbon), not trigonal pyramidal, so option A is incorrect. Carbon in COCl₂ is sp² hybridised, not sp³, so option C is incorrect. Both CO and COCl₂ are diamagnetic (no unpaired electrons), so option D is incorrect. Hence only option B is correct.",
